From 1d186f437ceb60b3d8ddd3aca15852e97c06c8e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:22:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: the help of videoscreen.hades3doutput says what
 happens

The help said "while Kodi shows a video" (it is while Kodi draws in a
split 3D mode, with a video or without), "whatever was asked for" (a
mode chosen in the settings is drawn as chosen), "as before" for Off
(the 3D modes of a display are no longer among the resolutions, whatever
this setting says) and "from the next change of the 3D mode" (it is the
next time a mode is set).

It did not say that frame packing for a film needs the refresh rate to
follow the video, that the display has to be on when Kodi starts, or
that one more change of mode is to be expected.

English, and the three Spanish files of Estuary ("dividido" for
"partido"). The source file of the skin gets the msgstr line that was
missing after this text.
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po           | 2 +-
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po  | 3 ++-
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 5 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index 230c04b..4b67670 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -25225,7 +25225,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hades3doutput"; translated in Estuary (#31712)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#39978"
-msgid "With a 3D TV or projector. While Kodi shows a video in a split 3D mode (over/under or side by side), the display is told so over HDMI and switches to 3D by itself. Frame packing, which keeps both eyes at full resolution, is used where the display and the graphics driver have it (Kodi then draws over/under, whatever was asked for); else the half format that is drawn. The refresh rate is the one the video gets anyway. Off: the two halves go out as an ordinary 2D picture and the display is switched to 3D by hand, as before. Turn it off if a 3D video shows a black or broken picture. Without a 3D display nothing changes. Applies from the next change of the 3D mode."
+msgid "For a 3D TV or projector. While Kodi draws in a split 3D mode (over/under or side by side), the display is told so over HDMI and switches to 3D by itself. Frame packing, which keeps both eyes at full resolution, is used where the display and the graphics driver have it (Kodi then draws over/under, also for a side-by-side video); else the half format that is drawn. The refresh rate is the one the video gets anyway: for a film in frame packing, turn on the adjustment of the display's refresh rate to the video, because HDMI has frame packing for 1080p at 24 Hz only. The display has to be on when Kodi starts. Expect one more change of display mode when a 3D video starts and when it stops. Off: the two halves go out as an ordinary 2D picture and the display is switched to 3D by hand. Turn it off if a 3D video shows a black or broken picture. Without a 3D display nothing changes. Applies the next time the display mode is set."
 msgstr ""
 
 #. Hades: label of setting "videoscreen.hades3doutput"; translated in Estuary (#31711)
